{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/20089","id":3367067678,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLCAjRs7IsWAe","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/20089","diff_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/20089.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/20089.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/20089","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/20089/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/20089/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/20089/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/statuses/7b8dacbc1c57aa72ae34c9449b23b69765d3a46e","number":20089,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: [1/2] [DeepEP] Fuse shared expert into MoE dispatch under EP","user":{"login":"xutizhou","id":185465032,"node_id":"U_kgDOCw34yA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/185465032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou","html_url":"https://github.com/xutizhou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xutizhou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\n<!-- Describe the purpose and goals of this pull request. -->\r\n\r\nIn DeepSeek V3/R1 with expert parallelism (EP), each rank currently computes the shared expert **separately** from routed experts. This means shared expert is not part of the DeepEP dispatch/compute/combine pipeline — it runs as a standalone forward pass on every rank.\r\n\r\nThis PR fuses the shared expert into the MoE path by treating it as an additional routed expert (the \"9th expert\" per rank). Instead of computing shared expert separately, it is dispatched through DeepEP alongside routed experts, assigned to the source rank's local shared expert slot.\r\n\r\nThis is the **first half** of the waterfill feature split (requested by @ch-wan in #19290):\r\n- **[1/2] This PR**: Fuse shared expert into DeepEP dispatch (fixed local assignment)\r\n- **[2/2] Follow-up PR**: Add waterfill load balancing to dynamically assign shared expert to the least-loaded rank\r\n\r\ncoauthor: @AichenF\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\n**New file: `python/sglang/srt/layers/moe/deepep_shared_expert_fusion.py`** (65 lines)\r\n- `LOCAL_SHARED_MARKER`: sentinel value for invalid expert ID (DeepEP ignores `expert_id < 0`)\r\n- `expand_topk_with_shared_expert()`: expands topk output `[N, 8] → [N, 9]` with expert ID remapping and shared expert always assigned to source rank\r\n\r\n**Modified files:**\r\n\r\n- **`models/deepseek_v2.py`** (+138/−22):\r\n  - Adjusts `num_experts` and `top_k` to account for extra shared expert slots (`+ep_size` experts, `+1` topk)\r\n  - Skips standalone shared expert forward when fusion is enabled\r\n  - Calls `expand_topk_with_shared_expert()` after TopK selection to append shared expert column\r\n  - Allows shared expert fusion under EP when `--enable-deepep-waterfill` is set (bypasses existing EP disable checks)\r\n\r\n- **`layers/moe/fused_moe_triton/layer.py`** (+40/−2):\r\n  - Expert ID remapping in weight loading: maps checkpoint expert IDs to expanded layout (original routed experts + 1 shared expert slot per rank)\r\n  - Adjusts shared expert detection threshold for the expanded expert ID space\r\n\r\n- **`server_args.py`** (+29/−1):\r\n  - Adds `--enable-deepep-waterfill` CLI flag with validation (requires `moe_a2a_backend='deepep'`)\r\n  - Updates `--disable-shared-experts-fusion` help text\r\n\r\n## Usage\r\n\r\n```bash\r\npython3 -m sglang.launch_server \\\r\n    --model-path <DeepSeek-V3-path> \\\r\n    --tp 16 --dp-size 16 --nnodes 2 --node-rank {0|1} \\\r\n    --dist-init-addr <addr>:<port> \\\r\n    --moe-a2a-backend deepep --deepep-mode normal \\\r\n    --enable-dp-attention \\\r\n    --enable-deepep-waterfill\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\n<!-- If this pull request affects model outputs (e.g., changes to the kernel or model forward code), provide accuracy test results. -->\r\n\r\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\r\n\r\n<!-- If this pull request impacts inference speed, provide benchmarking and profiling results. -->\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [ ] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the PR flow. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`, `/tag-and-rerun-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls to merge.\r\n","labels":[{"id":6403845273,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAABfbLsmQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true},{"id":8072782154,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAAB4SzhSg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/labels/deepseek","name":"deepseek","description":"","color":"c2e0c6","default":false},{"id":9283445059,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLCAjRs8AAAACKVYhQw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/labels/run-ci","name":"run-ci","description":"","color":"9FE30D","default":false}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-03-07T08:54:46Z","updated_at":"2026-04-09T08:48:28Z","closed_at":"2026-04-09T08:48:28Z","merged_at":"2026-04-09T08:48:28Z","merge_commit_sha":"57ffc55fb647bfc241d8c4766b846f4243b9c81d","assignee":{"login":"ch-wan","id":54331508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzMxNTA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54331508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ch-wan","html_url":"https://github.com/ch-wan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ch-wan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ch-wan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ch-wan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ch-wan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ch-wan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://a